projectId: fed-2026
config: config.toon
styles: styles/theme.toon
narration:
  fullTranscript: "July 29, 2026. The Federal Reserve held rates at three and a half to three and three quarter percent. A hold was the base case. What surprised the market was the vote. Nine to three. The most divided committee since 2016. Three policymakers dissented, calling for a quarter-point hike. The chair called it a review, not a pause. Now read the statement as a trader would. Target range unchanged. Inflation still above two percent. And a committee that won't waver. The market moved within minutes. Stocks fell. The thirty-year Treasury yield jumped to its highest since 2007, at five point eight four percent. Oil rose. The dollar softened. Crypto barely moved. The long end is doing the tightening the Fed refused to do. Here are the numbers that matter. The thirty-year at five point eight four. September hike odds near one in three. Tech down after seven of the last eight meetings. Financials earning on a higher net interest margin. So here is the playbook. Fade the tech sell-the-news tilt. Tilt long financials on the margin tailwind. Watch the thirty-year for the real tightening signal. Track oil and the dollar; the Iran shock sets the headline risk. And keep September sixteenth hedges on. Until then, trade the divergence."
  entries[7]{id,text}:
    n1,"July 29, 2026. The Federal Reserve held rates at three and a half to three and three quarter percent. A hold was the base case."
    n2,"What surprised the market was the vote. Nine to three. The most divided committee since 2016. Three policymakers dissented, calling for a quarter-point hike."
    n3,"The chair called it a review, not a pause. Now read the statement as a trader would. Target range unchanged. Inflation still above two percent. And a committee that won't waver."
    n4,"The market moved within minutes. Stocks fell. The thirty-year Treasury yield jumped to its highest since 2007, at five point eight four percent. Oil rose. The dollar softened. Crypto barely moved. The long end is doing the tightening the Fed refused to do."
    n5,"Here are the numbers that matter. The thirty-year at five point eight four. September hike odds near one in three. Tech down after seven of the last eight meetings. Financials earning on a higher net interest margin."
    n6,"So here is the playbook. Fade the tech sell-the-news tilt. Tilt long financials on the margin tailwind. Watch the thirty-year for the real tightening signal. Track oil and the dollar; the Iran shock sets the headline risk. And keep September sixteenth hedges on."
    n7,"Until then, trade the divergence."
